Description: obs-websocket: SetVideoSettings resets the video on the UI thread
 SetVideoSettings called obs_frontend_reset_video() on obs-websocket's own request thread (a Qt thread pool's), and the
 frontend's reset runs OBSBasic::ResetVideo() where it is called: it resizes the preview and the program view
 (ResizePreview, ResizeProgram read and set the widgets), updates the multiview projectors and enables a menu action,
 and Qt allows that only on the main thread ("QWidget and all its subclasses, are not reentrant. They can only be used
 from the main thread", Qt 6, Threads and QObjects). Measured on OBS 33.0.1 under gdb (a breakpoint on
 OBSBasic::ResetVideo with "info threads"): each of three SetVideoSettings requests ran the reset on "Thread (pooled)"
 (QThreadPoolThread::run, WebSocketServer::ProcessMessage, RequestHandler::SetVideoSettings), only the start-up reset on
 OBS's main thread. With this patch all four resets ran on OBS's main thread (thread 1 "obs"), the three requests
 answered and their canvases read back, and no Qt warning came off the main thread.
 The reset is queued inside the UI thread, as obs-websocket's own UI requests queue theirs (SetStudioModeEnabled) and
 patch 0012 queues a hotkey triggered by name, and waited for unless the request runs on the graphics thread (a
 SerialFrame batch), which the UI thread may itself be waiting for. The other requests that reach the frontend were read:
 the frontend queues theirs to the main thread itself (QMetaObject::invokeMethod), the handler queues them
 (SetCurrentSceneCollection, SetCurrentProfile, SetStudioModeEnabled), or they reach no widget.
 obs-websocket issue 1344 reports another fault through the same request (an inactive output's stale video pointer
 after the reset); this patch does not touch it.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS (ORDER 61, milestone 3, continuation 7)
Forwarded: no, OBS asks for human-written submissions only (CONTRIBUTING.md, AI/Machine Learning Policy)
Last-Update: 2026-11-23
---
diff --git a/obs-websocket-5-7-6/src/requesthandler/RequestHandler_Config.cpp b/obs-websocket-5-7-6/src/requesthandler/RequestHandler_Config.cpp
index c97eb51..584c1a4 100644
--- a/obs-websocket-5-7-6/src/requesthandler/RequestHandler_Config.cpp
+++ b/obs-websocket-5-7-6/src/requesthandler/RequestHandler_Config.cpp
@@ -511,7 +511,13 @@ RequestResult RequestHandler::SetVideoSettings(const Request &request)
 
 	if (changeFps || changeBaseRes || changeOutputRes) {
 		config_save_safe(config, "tmp", nullptr);
-		obs_frontend_reset_video();
+		// The frontend's video reset resizes the preview and the program view, updates the multiview projectors and
+		// enables a menu action, which Qt allows only on the main thread. Queue the task inside of the UI thread to
+		// prevent race conditions, and wait for it unless this request runs on the graphics thread (a SerialFrame
+		// batch), which the UI thread may itself be waiting for.
+		obs_queue_task(
+			OBS_TASK_UI, [](void *) { obs_frontend_reset_video(); }, nullptr,
+			!obs_in_task_thread(OBS_TASK_GRAPHICS));
 		return RequestResult::Success();
 	}
 
